[0.065, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[G\r\n\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m⏺\u001b[39m Here's what I found:\r\n\r\n  \u001b[1mOverview\u001b[22m\r\n\r\n  This is a \u001b[1mpresentation repository for QCon San Francisco 2025\u001b[22m about \"Engineering at\r\n  AI Speed\" - a talk about building \u001b]8;;https://claude.com/claude-code\u0007\u001b[34mhttps://claude.com/claude-code\u001b[39m\u001b]8;;\u0007 (Anthropic's CLI) \u001b]8;;\u0007\r\n  using AI assistance. The key insight: \u001b[1m90% of Claude Code was written with or by \u001b[22m\r\n  \u001b[1mClaude Code itself\u001b[22m.\r\n\r\n  \u001b[1mRepository Structure\u001b[22m\r\n\r\n  \u001b[1mCore Components:\u001b[22m\r\n  - \u001b[38;2;177;185;249msrc/\u001b[39m - Custom terminal-based presentation system (renderer, parser, ANSI handling,\r\n  asciinema player)\r\n  - \u001b[38;2;177;185;249mstatic/presentation.md\u001b[39m - The actual slide deck\r\n  - \u001b[38;2;177;185;249mdemos/\u001b[39m - Live code demos (cursor performance, SQLite issues, shell pipes, etc.)\r\n  - \u001b[38;2;177;185;249mscripts/presentation.ts\u001b[39m - Main presentation runner\r\n  - \u001b[38;2;177;185;249"]
[0.000, "o", "mstatic/*.cast\u001b[39m - Asciinema recordings for demos\r\n  - \u001b[38;2;177;185;249mstatic/*.txt\u001b[39m - ASCII art assets\r\n\r\n  \u001b[1mTech Stack:\u001b[22m\r\n  - Bun + TypeScript\r\n  - Custom markdown parser and renderer\r\n  - tmux integration for live demos\r\n  - asciicinema for terminal recordings\r\n\r\n  \u001b[1mCurrent State\u001b[22m\r\n\r\n  Modified files (per git status):\r\n  - \u001b[38;2;177;185;249mscripts/presentation.ts\u001b[39m - Modified\r\n  - \u001b[38;2;177;185;249mstatic/presentation.md\u001b[39m - Modified\r\n  - Several new \u001b[38;2;177;185;249m.cast\u001b[39m files and a \u001b[38;2;177;185;249mclaude\u001b[39m binary\r\n\r\n  \u001b[1mThe Talk's Theme\u001b[22m\r\n\r\n  Three real stories from building Claude Code:\r\n  1. \u001b[1mText Input (🎯)\u001b[22m - 333→945 lines over 9 months, Unicode handling\r\n  2. \u001b[1mShell Execution (🐚)\u001b[22m - Pivoted from persistent to transient shells\r\n  3. \u001b[1mSQLite Storage (🗄️)\u001b[22m - Shipped and removed in 15 days\r\n\r\n  \u001b[1mCore message\u001b[22m: \"Implementation is becoming free. Feedback loops are becoming\r\n  everything.\"\r\n\r\n  The presentation sys"]
[0.000, "o", "tem itself appears to be a custom-built terminal UI with\r\n  interactive navigation, live demos, and ASCII art rendering!\r\n\r\n\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m∴ Thought for 5s (\u001b[1mctrl+o\u001b[22m to show thinking)\u001b[39m\r\n\r\n\u001b[38;2;215;119;87m*\u001b[39m \u001b[38;2;235;159;127mEva\u001b[38;2;215;119;87mporating… \u001b[38;2;153;153;153m(\u001b[1mesc \u001b[22mto interrupt)\u001b[39m\r\n\r\n\u001b[2m\u001b[38;2;177;185;249m───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[39m\u001b[22m\r\n\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m> \u001b[39m\u001b[7m \u001b[27m\r\n\u001b[2m\u001b[38;2;177;185;249m───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[39m\u001b[22m\r\n  \u001b[38;2;153;153;153m~/.claude/t"]
